  "final_text": "All four steps are done.\n\n1. The data view's time field is `timestamp`.\n2. I created the dashboard 'S4-4605d0a6 Flights' with two panels: \"Flights over time\" (a line chart of the flight count by `timestamp`) and \"Flights per carrier\" (a bar chart of the flight count by `Carrier`).\n3. I created the rule 'S4-4605d0a6 Cancelled flights' as an `.es-query` rule on `kibana_sample_data_flights`. It runs every minute and fires when more than 10 documents with `Cancelled: true` arrive in a 5-minute window. It was created disabled, so I enabled it.\n4. I renamed the carrier panel to 'Flights by carrier'. I didn't re-read the dashboard after the rename, so the new title isn't confirmed beyond the update succeeding. I then read the rule back: it shows as enabled with status \"ok\".\n\nTIME_FIELD: timestamp\nRULE_ENABLED: yes",
